From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:27:16 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: dw9719: reach the focus position on resume

dw9719_resume() ramps the lens back to the focus control's value in
steps of DW9719_CTRL_STEPS, starting at the remainder of the value. The
loop stops before it writes the value itself, so the lens is left one
step (16 codes) short of the position user space set, until the next
control write: at 450 the ramp ends at 434.

Run the loop up to and including the control's value. For a value of
0 the one extra write is 0, the position the lens has after power-up.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/dw9719.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/dw9719.c b/drivers/media/i2c/dw9719.c
index 7ea976df9247..22ae711d7cd3 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/dw9719.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/dw9719.c
@@ -304,7 +304,7 @@ static int dw9719_resume(struct device *dev)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	for (val = current_focus % DW9719_CTRL_STEPS; val < current_focus;
+	for (val = current_focus % DW9719_CTRL_STEPS; val <= current_focus;
 	     val += DW9719_CTRL_STEPS) {
 		ret = dw9719_t_focus_abs(dw9719, val);
 		if (ret)
